Deloitte DevOps Engineer Interview Experience
Recently went through a DevOps Engineer interview process, and it was a really insightful experience that tested both practical knowledge and real-world problem solving.
Here are some of the key areas and questions discussed 👇
🔹 CI/CD & Jenkins
Designed end-to-end CI/CD pipeline
Declarative vs Scripted pipelines
Jenkins triggers, webhooks, and Shared Libraries
Debugging pipelines when builds don’t trigger
🔹 Docker & Kubernetes
Docker image build lifecycle (ENTRYPOINT vs CMD)
Kubernetes architecture (Control Plane vs Worker Nodes)
Troubleshooting: CrashLoopBackOff, ImagePullBackOff
Helm chart structure and deployments
Accessing and managing running pods
🔹 Cloud (AWS)
Working with EC2, EKS, ECS, and container registries
Connecting to ECS containers
Secure communication with databases
🔹 Terraform & Automation
Creating and managing infrastructure using Terraform
Reusable and scalable infrastructure design
🔹 Advanced DevOps Practices
Branching strategies (GitFlow vs Trunk-based)
Handling production issues and hotfix releases
End-to-end deployment flow (Code → Build → Deploy → Monitor)
🔹 Security & Best Practices
Docker image vulnerability scanning
Managing secrets securely in EKS
Environment variable handling
Helm chart signing & secure deployments
